  "prefLabel": "Pes 202.17 Conduct of Parties and Representatives",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Pes 202.17 Conduct of Parties and Representatives. In the interest of order and decorum, if the presiding officer determines that cross-examination is disruptive to the orderly conduct of the proceedings, the presiding officer shall require cross-examination to be conducted indirectly, by addressing questions through the presiding officer.\n\nSource. #5590, eff 2-25-93; ss by #6258, eff 5-30-96; ss by #8058, eff 5-30-04; ss by #10198-A, eff 10-3-12",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/pes200.html"
